# ADR-002: Use a Custom Amazon VPC

## Status

Accepted

## Context

Amazon EKS requires networking for worker nodes, load balancers, and communication between Kubernetes components. The application also contains stateful workloads and must be isolated from the public internet.

## Decision

A custom VPC will be created specifically for the EKS platform.

The VPC will span three Availability Zones and contain separate public and private subnets.

## Rationale

Using a dedicated VPC provides:

- Network isolation
- Fine-grained routing control
- Secure private workloads
- Multi-AZ resilience
- Support for Kubernetes networking

## Alternatives Considered

### Default AWS VPC

Pros:
- Faster to start
- Already exists

Cons:
- Shared configuration
- Poor separation
- Not representative of production

### Custom VPC

Pros:
- Full control
- Better security
- Production design
- Easier to manage

Cons:
- More resources
- More networking knowledge required

## Consequences

All platform resources will be deployed inside this VPC.

Networking decisions such as routing, subnet placement, security groups, and internet access will be controlled by this design.